+# Exact remaining reference-profile and closure inputs
+
+[reference-profile-inputs.json](reference-profile-inputs.json) expands the opaque component/closure-profile slots into their actual members, accountable owner and next action. All values remain null: the bundle contains no installed profile, enrollment or qualified physical backend. These are infrastructure-only reference-backend inputs, not an adopted AWS requirement or application-native identifiers.
+
+The list includes account/region/table ARN and immutable table ID; each archive bucket owner and exact enrollment key/version/hash with numeric retention/extension evidence; every tenant/source/successor/tainted epoch and KEK protector identity mapping; original encrypted KEK context/version; separately governed public trust/current revocation; exact independently enrolled owner scope/genesis and checkpoint ancestry; administrator/deputy recovery/fencing; and measured transport, closure and completion capacity. Socket ownership, disabled swap/core/memory capture and exact native grants require installed evidence, not template assertions.
+
+Every copy class has an accountable actual owner and independently authenticated coverage, including empty classes. Every copy records location, process, lineage, epoch/root reference, immutable outcome and closure evidence. Each producer/queue must reconcile every admitted sequence/native intent. Every actual caller/SDK/sidecar/UDS/gRPC/TLS/component/native holder is enrolled before release; exact observer completion binds its process and transport incarnation and original admission. Local key disposal clears only the owned array. It does not prove remote buffers, hidden copies or irreversible deletion.
+
+[source-dispositions.json](source-dispositions.json) separately names missing owning-service implementations and the EventStore source/package/production integration, whose owner is the **EventStore Maintainer**. Interfaces, image names, environment variables and credential references do not close missing source. The current sibling source used by local conformance builds is not an accepted installed dependency target.
+
+The deduplicated top-level [installation-input-ledger-reviewed.json](installation-input-ledger-reviewed.json) has one entry per input, combining multiple unmet conditions in its reason. Earlier ledgers remain intermediate evidence. The [prior semantic-provider gaps](../ext-secrets-1-semantic-provider-2026-10-22/final-installation-gaps.json) and [EventStore handback](../ext-secrets-1-semantic-provider-2026-10-22/EVENTSTORE-HANDBACK.md) remain historical evidence, unchanged; this companion does not relabel them as installed.
